      "text": "Ryosuke drove $74592-74568=24$ miles. This means that he uses $\\frac{24}{28}=\\frac{6}{7}$ gallons of gas. Each gallon is $4.05$ so $\\frac{6}{7}$ gallons is $\\left(\\frac{6}{7}\\right)\\times 4.05=3.571428571\\dots$$=\\boxed{\\$3.57}$\n\nProblem:\nFind the complete expansion and sum of the expression $(x+y)(z+w)$.\n\nSolution:\nFirst, expand each part of the expression, and then combine like terms. This will yield $$\\begin{array}{rcl}(x+y)(z+w) &= &x(x+z) + x(y+w) + y(z+w) \\\\ &= &x^2+xz+xy+xw+yz+yw \\end{array}$$ When we sum this with $(x+y)$, we get \\begin{align} (x+y)(z+w) + (x+y) &= (xz+xw) + (y^2+yw) + (yz+yx) \\\\ &= (x^2+xz+xy) + (y^2+xy+yw) \\\\ \\end{align} Since $yw = w(y+1) = w+yw$, the answer is \\begin{align} (x+y)(z+w) + (x+y) &= (x^2+xz+xy) + (y^2+yw) + (yz+yx) \\\\ &= x^2 +xz-1+w+y^2-yw \\\\ &= x^2+y^2 + xz+yx+yw \\text{.} \\end{align} We finished the expansion and summed the complete answer at the very end.\n\nProblem:\nIf $n = a + b = b + c = c+a$, compute $(a+b+c)(a^2+b^2+c^2-ab-bc-ca)$.\n\nSolution:\nTo find a systematic approach to solve the problem, we use the knowledge from first grade. Let's start with the equation:\n\nGiven that $n = a + b = b + c = c + a$, this suggests that $a, b,$ and $c$ can be expressed as $a = b - n$, $b = c - n$, and $c = a - n$.\n\nBy substituting these values for $a$, $b$, and $c$ into the expression $(a+b+c)(a^2+b^2+c^2-abc)$, we get:\n\n$a+b+c = (b-n)+(c-n)+(a-n) = (a+b+c)-3n$\n\nNow, substitute back into the expression to find:\n\n$a^2+b^2+c^2-abc = a^2+b^2+c^2-(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)$, \n\ntherefore, the original expression simplifies to $8(n^3-n^2)$, which is equivalent to $8a^3-8a^2$\n\nWe can verify that the formula is correct by accepting the fact that the expansion formula can solve many math formulas\n\nConsider that all of the cubes are rooted at the vertices and shapes are side by side. The solution can be attained by iterating through the vertices and checking each one to see if they form an edge with another circle: For each circle, iterate through its vertices, and for each circle, check if it shares an edge with another circle using the is_edge() function defined below. The function works as follows: It takes two edges and determines if they intersect or touch (i.e., if they are on the same line). Two vertices are a neighboring vertex of the first edge if there are no other edges connecting one of the vertices and the second edge. Finally, for each… Read Ans: On a Friday, Courtney earns 5% of the profits from her lemonade stand each hour. Her total earnings from the lemonade stand are $50/10 to $X, Which is her hourly rate. Courtney earned How much on the $55 For the previous weekday, Addison paid Kayden $200/ hour for time worked. Today Addison gets paid 1.5 times $200, but she worked for only 7 hours of regular time. Addison paid Kayden (200*$X/2 hours) * 1.0 X = $20 On the previous weekday, Addison’s pay for working X time is 200*X, so she’s been paid 200*X-160 80 is the number of dollars she earned. On the previous day, Addison’s pay for working X time is 200*X, so she’s been paid 200*X-80 160 is the number of dollars she earned. How many dollars will Kayden get today?\n\nProfessor Rosenthal keeps running, but then slows down and walks at a steady rate for the last half of the distance each lap. If she does 5 laps, her total journey was 7.2 miles long. How far was the last lap that Rosenthal walked?\n\nSolution:\nShe did $7.2*2*5 = 72$ miles total. So from this we are finding the distance from $36/14 = \\frac{9}{3.5}$ (Since she walks half as far each lap) half way through, so: $9 miles*3$ half min npk middle lap to the $14/$10*$10*1 = 9km$ far loop. 10m asterix $9/8 = 11.25m$ Could you answer this question? 22 years old man 30 years old man 20 years old girl in 1st one 20 years older in 2nd one 11 years older in 3rd one\n\nHey there! In the problems below, you will have to make 3 grids. Well, just learned this today so try it! Can you finish